meta {
  name: Update profile
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/me/profile
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "firstName": "Max",
    "headline": "Backend developer",
    "locationId": null,
    "preferencesLocationIds": ["{{locationId}}","{{locationId1}}","{{locationId2}}"],
    "yearsExperience": 4.5,
    "seniority": "MID",
    "skills": [
      { "slug": "typescript", "level": "ADVANCED", "yearsExperience": 3 },
      { "slug": "nestjs", "level": "INTERMEDIATE" },
      { "slug": "postgresql" }
    ],
    "industries": ["artificial-intelligence"],
    "preferences": {
      "remotePreference": "HYBRID",
      "surelyemploymentType": "FULL_TIME",
      "minSalary": 60000,
      "salaryCurrency": "EUR",
      "willingToRelocate": true
    }
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  locationId: 47f03b00-eeae-4bcc-8c84-c71505c0e90a
  locationId1: 64392f03-80d2-4e68-ab51-8cdf43b0d10c
  locationId2: 06f7c3b1-7e77-46e5-97b9-15362655ad93
}

docs {
  Send only what changes. Returns the full updated profile.
  
  - Omitted field: unchanged. `null`: clears it (not firstName/lastName).
  - `locationId`: an id from **List locations**, e.g. `"{{locationId}}"`.
    `null` here keeps onboarding incomplete; set an id to complete it.
  - `skills` / `industries`: replace the whole list; `[]` clears it.
    Skills and industries are referenced by slug (see List skills/industries).
  - `industries` order sets the priority (first = 1).
  - `preferencesLocationIds`: replaces the whole list (max 4, unique); ids from
    **List locations**, which stores the first three results as `locationId`,
    `locationId1`, `locationId2` (run it first). `[]` clears it.
  - `preferences`: merged into the saved preferences.
  - Enums: remotePreference REMOTE | HYBRID | ONSITE;
    employmentType FULL_TIME | PART_TIME | CONTRACT | INTERNSHIP | FREELANCE;
    level BEGINNER | INTERMEDIATE | ADVANCED | EXPERT;
    seniority INTERN | JUNIOR | MID | SENIOR | LEAD.
  - 400: invalid body, unknown skill/industry slug or location id · 401: run Login
  - onboardingCompleted is computed by the server: true only while headline (Q1 roles) and location (Q2) are both set, otherwise false.
}
